                <h2>The Good News</h2>
                <span class="ornament">✦</span>
            </div>

            <div class="scripture-card reveal">
                <p class="lead">
                    <span class="dropcap">G</span>od created man: Adam (the first man) and his wife Eve
                    (the first woman). Adam and Eve sinned in the Garden of Eden after listening to the
                    serpent; he convinced them to eat the forbidden fruit of the knowledge of good and evil.
                </p>
                <p>
                    After that sin, man was separated from God. We all inherit this sinful nature from Adam
                    and Eve, which creates a separation from God who is Holy. This separation puts us in hell
                    when we die&mdash;but God did not want that, because He loves us. So He sent His only Son,
                    <strong>Jesus Christ</strong>, to live a life of no sin and die on the cross as a sacrifice
                    for our sins.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Jesus was raised from the dead after three days and is alive forevermore. We can now choose
                    Jesus as our Lord and Savior and have a relationship with Father God. The only way to get
                    saved is by the blood of Jesus&mdash;accepting the sacrifice He made for us, repenting, and
                    giving our life to Him.
                </p>
                <p class="closing-line">For by grace are ye saved through faith. <span class="ref">— Ephesians 2:8</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
