            <!-- What We Believe / Statement of Faith -->
            <section id="beliefs" class="beliefs section">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="section-head">
                        <span class="ornament">✦</span>
                        <h2>What We Believe</h2>
                        <span class="ornament">✦</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="section-sub">Our Statement of Faith — the foundation of all we teach and live by.</p>

                    <div class="belief-grid">
                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Bible (The Holy Scriptures)</h3>
                            <p>The Bible (Composed of the Old Testament and the New Testament) is the inspired, infallible, and inerrant Word of God — written by men moved by the Holy Spirit — as Christians, we live by these scriptures.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">2 Timothy 3:16-17 · 2 Peter 1:20-21 · Hebrews 4:12</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Triune God</h3>
                            <p>One true living God, YHWH, the Great I AM, Creator of Heaven and Earth, eternally existing in three co-equal, co-eternal persons: the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Genesis 1:26 · Matthew 28:19 · 2 Corinthians 13:14</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>God the Father</h3>
                            <p>God the Father is the Creator and Sustainer of all life, who lovingly adopts born again believers as His children.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Romans 8:15-17 · 1 John 3:1</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Jesus Christ, the Son of God</h3>
                            <p>Jesus Christ is the eternal Son of God, fully God and fully man, born of a virgin and without sin, who came to redeem creation and reconcile us to the Father.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Isaiah 7:14 · Matthew 1:18-23 · John 1:1-5 · John 14:6</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Holy Spirit</h3>
                            <p>The Holy Spirit is the third person of the Godhead — our comforter, counselor, teacher, and helper — who convicts the world of sin and empowers believers to be witnesses of Jesus.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">John 14:16-17, 26 · Acts 1:8 · John 16:7-8</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Blood and Resurrection of Jesus</h3>
                            <p>Jesus died on the cross, bearing our sin and punishment, was buried, and rose again in victory with the keys of hell and the grave. He ascended to the Father and lives to make intercession for us. Only by His blood are we redeemed.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Matthew 12:40 · Colossians 1:14 · Hebrews 9:22 · Romans 8:34</span>
                        </article>


                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Gospel and Salvation</h3>
                            <p>Salvation is the free gift of God, received by grace through wholehearted faith and surrender to the Lordship of Jesus Christ — believing He died for our sins and rose again — accompanied by genuine repentance.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">John 3:16 · Ephesians 2:8-9 · Romans 10:9-10 · Acts 2:38</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Water Baptism</h3>
                            <p>Water baptism is the outward declaration of dying with Christ and rising with Him in newness of life, uniting the believer with His death, burial, and resurrection.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Matthew 28:19 · Romans 6:3-11</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Baptism in the Holy Spirit</h3>
                            <p>The Baptism of the Holy Spirit empowers believers to be witnesses to the nations, and that praying in a heavenly language (known as Tongues) is one evidence of being filled with the Spirit.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Acts 1:4-8 · Acts 2:1-4</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Communion</h3>
                            <p>Communion is the sacred participation in the body and blood of Christ, by which we remember His sacrifice and proclaim His death until He comes.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Luke 22:19-20 · 1 Corinthians 10:16-17</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Gifts and Fruit of the Spirit</h3>
                            <p>Every believer is given gifts of the Spirit to minister to others and advance the Gospel, and that the true mark of a believer is the fruit of the Spirit reflecting Christ's character.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">1 Corinthians 12:7-11 · Romans 12:6-8 · Galatians 5:22-23</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Sanctification</h3>
                            <p>Sanctification is the ongoing work of God's grace that teaches us to walk in righteousness and purity, transforming us into the image of Christ.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Romans 12:1-2 · 1 Thessalonians 5:23 · Hebrews 13:12</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Great Commission</h3>
                            <p>Every believer is commanded to preach the Gospel, walk in the power of the Spirit, and make disciples of all nations.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Matthew 28:18-20 · Mark 16:15-18</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Church and Five-Fold Ministry</h3>
                            <p>The Church is the Body of Christ, the temple of God through the Holy Spirit, and that He gave the five-fold ministry — Apostle, Prophet, Evangelist, Pastor, and Teacher — to equip the saints for the work of ministry.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Ephesians 1:22-23 · Ephesians 4:11-15</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>Love</h3>
                            <p>Love is necessary and powerful, the two greatest commandments are to love the Lord with ALL our heart, soul, and mind, and to love our neighbor as ourselves.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Matthew 22:37-40 · 1 John 4:7-8</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Sanctity of Marriage</h3>
                            <p>The sanctity of marriage is a covenant between one man and one woman, and that we are called to walk in holiness and purity before the Lord.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Genesis 2:24 · Hebrews 13:4 · 1 Peter 1:15-16</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Hope of Our Salvation: The Rapture</h3>
                            <p>The rapture (A latin word) or Greek verb is harpazō (ἁρπάζω) is also known as the resurrection of the dead in Christ and their gathering, together with those who are alive, at the coming of the Lord — this is the blessed hope of our salvation.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">1 Thessalonians 4:16-17 · 1 Corinthians 15:51-55</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>The Final Judgment</h3>
                            <p>There will be a FINAL judgment in which all will be judged according to their works, and those not found written in the Book of Life will be separated from God forever.</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">Matthew 25:46 · Revelation 20:11-15</span>
                        </article>

                        <article class="belief-card reveal">
                            <h3>A New Heaven, New Earth, and a New Jerusalem</h3>
                            <p>The first heaven and the first earth will pass away, and God will create a new heaven, a new earth, and a new Jerusalem where righteousness dwells forever "And God shall wipe away every tear from their eyes."</p>
                            <span class="belief-ref">2 Peter 3:13 · Revelation 21:1</span>
                        </article>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

